{"chunk_id": "9853230fb099", "text": "At Draupadi\u2019s swayamvara, many powerful kings attempt to string a massive bow and strike a difficult target but fail. Karna, formidable and confident, prepares to shoot, yet Draupadi publicly refuses to accept a \"Suta\" (charioteer\u2019s son) as her husband, forcing him to withdraw despite his ability. Other renowned rulers such as Sisupala, Jarasandha, and Salya also fail to string the bow. When the Kshatriyas give up, Arjuna\u2014disguised as a Brahmana\u2014rises from among the Brahmins, provoking debate and skepticism among them. Calm and reverent, he salutes Shiva and remembers Krishna before effortlessly stringing the bow and shooting the target with five arrows. The arena erupts in divine and human celebration as Arjuna wins Draupadi, revealing both his unmatched skill and the hidden power of the Pandavas in exile.\nAt Draupadi\u2019s swayamvara, Arjuna\u2014disguised as a Brahmana\u2014strings the impossible bow and strikes the target, winning her after many kings fail.\nThemes: heroic prowess, disguise and identity, marriage contest, divine favor, royal rivalry", "vector": [-0.011691425926983356, -0.01680431328713894, -0.009523345157504082, 0.02109995111823082, -0.007855071686208248, 0.028178295120596886, -0.02603047713637352, -0.011461785063147545, -0.019830171018838882, -0.033095311373472214, 0.0014707151567563415, 0.0004943190142512321, -0.007780775427818298, 0.025854868814349174, 0.006460340227931738, 0.019897712394595146, 0.04225393384695053, -0.016290998086333275, 0.020127354189753532, -0.03682360053062439, 6.727762229274958e-05, -0.013555570505559444, -0.012184478342533112, 0.036472387611866, -0.029421057552099228, 0.026246609166264534, 0.012157461605966091, -0.02366652525961399, 0.013305666856467724, -0.006747391540557146, -0.0059875501319766045, 0.006629193667322397, -0.01071882899850607, -0.018236193805933, -0.03593205288052559, -0.013440749607980251, -0.007247197907418013, -0.019695088267326355, 0.0115